<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-f3yqd.2.23 (RDR-246 Activation Step 2, the first registered data move; RDR-229 Phase 1 decision D2, Sam 2026-11-20):
    registers the move repair-catalog-collection-model-version, which sets nexus.catalog_collections.model_version from the
    collection's conformant name where the column is ''. The census (T2 nexus_rdr/229-p1.2-census-2026-11-20) found 54 live rows
    at '' on the managed service: 12 on tenant nexus and 42 on gate-xr789, every one a conformant <type>__<owner>__<model>__v<N>
    name except gate-probe-124.

    THIS CHANGESET ONLY REGISTERS. One INSERT into nexus.data_moves, whatever the size of the table. It writes no
    catalog_collections row; the engine's move worker runs the repair after the engine serves, once per tenant, in batches
    (RDR-246, Technical Design). The policy that lets the migrating role read every tenant's rows to verify the move is the
    next changeset, in vectors-065-catalog-collections-owner-read.xml, never this one: a precondition skips its whole changeset,
    and its guard would skip this INSERT with it.

    THE TEMPLATE (what each chunk runs, with <driving_table> and <chunking_clause> filled in by dml_utils, alias t):
        UPDATE nexus.catalog_collections AS t
           SET model_version = substring(t.name from '__(v[0-9]+)$')
         WHERE <chunking_clause> AND t.model_version = '' AND t.name ~ '<rule>'
    <rule> is ^(quarantine-|)(code|docs|rdr|knowledge)__<owner>__<model>__v[0-9]+$ (the prefix is an optional group written as an alternation with an empty branch, since a question mark is barred) with the owner grammar
    [a-zA-Z0-9-]+(_[a-zA-Z0-9-]+)* and the model grammar [a-z][a-z0-9-]*. Without the optional quarantine- prefix it is the engine's
    own conformant-name rule (hygiene-002-1 branch A, hygiene-004-1's m4, the Java test helper's CONFORMANT_COLLECTION_NAME), which
    is src/nexus/corpus.py's _CONFORMANT_COLLECTION_RE, nothing looser; with it, hygiene-004-1's mq, the quarantine sibling's shape.
    The prefix is there so a quarantine sibling is repaired with its origin (see READERS below). The version is the name's last
    segment, so v01 stays v01, as corpus.py's parse_conformant_collection_name returns it. The owner's optional underscore run is
    written (_x)* and not (?:_x)*: the verification below may hold no question mark (the JDBC driver binds one), and the template
    uses the same text so the two cannot differ.

    NAMES THE MOVE LEAVES AS FOUND: anything the rule does not match (a legacy two-segment name such as docs__default,
    gate-probe-124, docs____m__v1 with an empty owner, docs__o__1m__v1 whose model starts with a digit, a name ending __v1x, a
    quarantine- prefix on a name that is not conformant). The move has no skipped-row counter, so the operator reads what is left
    with this query, run as nexus_admin (the migrating role reads every tenant's rows through vectors-065's policy):
        SELECT tenant_id, name FROM nexus.catalog_collections WHERE model_version = '' AND name !~ '^(quarantine-|)(code|docs|rdr|knowledge)__[a-zA-Z0-9-]+(_[a-zA-Z0-9-]+)*__[a-z][a-z0-9-]*__v[0-9]+$'
    nx catalog collections-census also counts them ("unusable model_versions"); it lands with RDR-229 P1.2.

    READERS DURING THE MOVE (RDR-246, Readers during a move). QuarantineOrigin.rowsOf matches a quarantine sibling to its origin by
    equal owner_id, embedding_model, model_version and content_type (its attribute arm; its other arm matches the reaper's sibling,
    quarantine- plus the origin's name, by name and is unaffected by model_version). The template repairs a sibling with its
    origin, each to the version its own name carries, so for a pair whose sibling name carries its origin's version both change
    together, and a tenant whose registry fits in one chunk (chunk_size 100000; the registry holds 171 and 42 rows on the two
    production tenants) repairs every pair in one transaction. A larger tenant would have a window between chunks, until
    completed_at, in which an origin is repaired and its sibling is not (chunks tile the primary key (tenant_id, name), and
    docs__x and quarantine-docs__x sort apart), and the attribute arm misses the sibling there. A sibling whose own name carries
    another version than its origin's is repaired to its own name's version and stops matching its origin by attributes; the
    census found no quarantine row at '' on either production tenant, and CatalogModelVersionRepairMoveIntegrationTest pins this
    case. collectionForTuple orders a '' version as 0 and the repaired value is the name's own version; the production census
    found 0 tuples whose winner changes. Any other reader falls back to the name's version until completed_at is set.

    CUT COUPLING. This move lands on develop only together with D1 (nexus-p2m1x.10: upsertCollection refuses a blank
    model_version) and P1.4 commit A (on develop at 7dd321122), as part of RDR-229's Phase 2 engine cut. Writers produce only the
    new shape from that cut on (RDR-246, Approach step 5). A blank conformant row written between a tenant's run and the
    verification is an old-shape row the verification finds, and it fails the move for good (a superseding move fixes it).

    LATER CHANGESETS ON catalog_collections. The data-move gate (rule 3) accepts a completion precondition on any move that drives
    the table, so a later RDR-229 changeset that drops or renames something on catalog_collections keeps the P3.1 stamp-move label
    the RDR prescribes. It must NOT name this repair move's label: if this move ever fails, an onFail="CONTINUE" precondition on
    its completed_at would skip the dependent changeset forever.

    WRITERS DURING THE MOVE (RDR-246, Approach step 5). The template leaves a row whose model_version is already set unchanged
    and rewrites a row from its own current name, so it is correct against a writer that updates or deletes rows meanwhile.

    THE VERIFICATION (one bind parameter, the tenant; READ ONLY; run per tenant and once table-wide): a name that matches the rule
    and is still at '' is a row the move missed.
        SELECT 1 FROM nexus.catalog_collections t WHERE t.model_version = '' AND t.name ~ '<rule>'
                  AND (t.tenant_id = $1 OR $1 IS NULL)
    A non-conformant empty is not in it, so gate-probe-124 and the like never fail the move.

    PARAMETERS. chunk_size 100000, sleep_ms 0, statement_timeout_ms 30000. The table is the collection registry: a few hundred
    rows across all tenants (171 on tenant nexus, 43 on gate-xr789), so a tenant's rows are one chunk, each chunk is one UPDATE
    of tiny rows, and the pause between chunks that throttles a large move has nothing to throttle. The chunk is large on
    purpose, so that a quarantine pair is repaired in one transaction (READERS above). 30 s bounds the verification SELECT on a table that small
    many times over. The move is per tenant, as RDR-246 prescribes for a tenant-scoped table: the worker lists the default
    tenant, every service_tokens tenant and every tenant holding rows, and runs the template under each one's nexus.tenant.

    No on_complete: nothing is left to finish once the verification is empty. Every tenant's batch commits on its own and a
    restart resumes at the first unfinished chunk. The registry row is the only thing written here.

    Rollback unregisters the move: it deletes the registry row. A repair that already ran is not undone, which is harmless:
    the value written is the one the collection's name already says. The dml_utils run records of a rolled-back move stay in
    dml_utils_data, and a later registration of the same label would find the run complete, run nothing, and verify.

    DATA EFFECT: this changeset writes one row to the global registry nexus.data_moves and changes no existing row. The move it
    registers (after the engine serves, in the background) sets model_version on the nexus.catalog_collections rows whose
    model_version is '' and whose name is conformant (or a quarantine- sibling of a conformant name), to the name's own trailing
    version; the rollback of this changeset removes the registration and does not undo a repair that ran.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="vectors-064-1" author="nexus-f3yqd.2.23">
        <comment>Register the data move repair-catalog-collection-model-version over nexus.catalog_collections (RDR-246, RDR-229 D2): one INSERT into nexus.data_moves, no policy, no catalog_collections row written. DATA EFFECT: one row added to the global registry nexus.data_moves; no existing row changes at boot. The registered move, run by the engine after it serves, sets model_version from the conformant name on rows where it is ''; the rollback unregisters the move and does not undo a repair that ran.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false"><![CDATA[
INSERT INTO nexus.data_moves (label, template, driving_schema, driving_table, chunk_size, sleep_ms,
                              statement_timeout_ms, verification, on_complete, changeset_id)
VALUES ('repair-catalog-collection-model-version',
        'UPDATE <driving_table> SET model_version = substring(t.name from ''__(v[0-9]+)$'') WHERE <chunking_clause> AND t.model_version = '''' AND t.name ~ ''^(quarantine-|)(code|docs|rdr|knowledge)__[a-zA-Z0-9-]+(_[a-zA-Z0-9-]+)*__[a-z][a-z0-9-]*__v[0-9]+$''',
        'nexus', 'catalog_collections', 100000, 0, 30000,
        'SELECT 1 FROM nexus.catalog_collections t WHERE t.model_version = '''' AND t.name ~ ''^(quarantine-|)(code|docs|rdr|knowledge)__[a-zA-Z0-9-]+(_[a-zA-Z0-9-]+)*__[a-z][a-z0-9-]*__v[0-9]+$'' AND (t.tenant_id = $1 OR $1 IS NULL)',
        NULL, 'vectors-064-1');
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql>DELETE FROM nexus.data_moves WHERE label = 'repair-catalog-collection-model-version'</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
